        "calls": 1,
        "title": "Agent turns stop on no progress and step ceiling raised to 600",
        "summary": "A new no-progress guard in packages/agent-runtime ends a root turn after 40 consecutive model steps that changed no file and produced no new tool result, surfacing the stop as a finished turn with the message in NO_PROGRESS_STOP_MESSAGE rather than a failure. The root step ceiling MAX_AGENT_STEPS_DEFAULT in common rises from 200 to 600, while spawned agents get their own lower MAX_SUBAGENT_STEPS_DEFAULT of 200 so that raising the root budget does not multiply the worst case when a root step spawns several subagents. The docs section How a turn ends on its own lays out the two limits and their exemption rules, and run-agent-step now logs an agent_step_ceiling metric with isSubagent so the ceiling hit is measurable.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "end-users",
        "evidence": "The diff adds `packages/agent-runtime/src/util/turn-progress.ts` defining `createTurnProgress` and `NO_PROGRESS_STOP_THRESHOLD = 40`, changes `MAX_AGENT_STEPS_DEFAULT` in `common/src/constants/agents.ts` from 200 to 600, introduces `MAX_SUBAGENT_STEPS_DEFAULT = 200`, and updates `packages/agent-runtime/src/run-agent-step.ts` to wire the no-progress check into the root loop and return `stepToolCalls` / `stepToolResults` from each step.",
        "userVisible": true,
        "confidence": "medium",
        "changes": [
          {
            "area": "Agent Runtime",
            "what": "Adds a no-progress turn guard: createTurnProgress in a new util tracks consecutive steps with no file change or new tool output and loopAgentSteps breaks the root loop at NO_PROGRESS_STOP_THRESHOLD, appending NO_PROGRESS_STOP_MESSAGE as the turn's last word.",
            "files": [
              "packages/agent-runtime/src/util/turn-progress.ts",
              "packages/agent-runtime/src/run-agent-step.ts"
            ]
          },
          {
            "area": "Shared/Core",
            "what": "MAX_AGENT_STEPS_DEFAULT raised from 200 to 600 and MAX_SUBAGENT_STEPS_DEFAULT introduced at 200, separating the root backstop from the per-spawned-agent ceiling.",
            "files": [
              "common/src/constants/agents.ts"
            ]
          },
          {
            "area": "Agent Runtime",
            "what": "createAgentState in spawn-agent-utils now sets stepsRemaining to MAX_SUBAGENT_STEPS_DEFAULT instead of the root MAX_AGENT_STEPS_DEFAULT, so subagents inherit a lower, independent cap.",
            "files": [
              "packages/agent-runtime/src/tools/handlers/tool/spawn-agent-utils.ts"
            ]
          },
          {
            "area": "Agent Runtime",
            "what": "isRejectedEdit in file-edit-loop is exported so turn-progress can treat a rejected file edit as no progress even when the edit varies.",
