        "calls": 1,
        "text": "The AI coding assistant now stops a task early if it has not changed any files or produced new information for forty consecutive steps, ending the session with a clear explanation instead of wasting your time and credits. The maximum number of steps the main assistant can take in a single turn has also tripled from 200 to 600, allowing complex jobs more room to finish before hitting a hard limit. For developers using the tool, this means stuck sessions will now halt gracefully with guidance on how to proceed, while productive but long-running tasks are less likely to be cut off prematurely.",
