        "calls": 1,
        "title": "Add archived chat restore error messages for Cloud and Desktop",
        "summary": "The desktop-cloud contract in common/ now defines three distinct error states for archived chats: one for standard archival where files can be restored by sending a message, one for cases where Cloud lost its copy but Desktop can restore from its export, and one for when no copy survives. The localRestoreRequired flag in CloudHistoryChat is documented to indicate that Cloud cannot bring back files but Desktop can land its saved export. These changes refine the wire contract for handling file restoration after archiving a Cloud chat.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "audience": "maintainers",
        "evidence": "In common/src/desktop-cloud/handback.ts, the diff adds two new error constants, ARCHIVED_CHAT_DESKTOP_ERROR and ARCHIVED_CHAT_LOST_ERROR, and updates the doc comment for ARCHIVED_CHAT_RESTORE_ERROR to clarify that archiving moves files to storage rather than permanently deleting them. In common/src/desktop-cloud/history.ts, the comment for localRestoreRequired is updated to state that Cloud cannot restore files but Desktop can land their export.",
        "userVisible": true,
        "confidence": "medium",
        "unknowns": "The diff does not show the server-side logic that determines which of the three error states is returned to the client.",
